ce is hand-finished in our Maryland workshop by skilled artisans.<\/p>","button_label":"","button_link":"","button_style":"btn","button_color":"btn--white"}}},"block_order":["text_block_XzL9y8","text_block_DcDL4E","text_block_r3dFt4"],"custom_css":[".image__fill.fade-in-image {padding-top: 20% !important;}",".background-size-cover.lazyloaded {background-size: contain !important; background-repeat: no-repeat;}",".section-columns.palette--light.bg--neutral {position: relative; background-image: url(\"https:\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0807\/9133\/9240\/files\/image_4.png?v=1789475682\"); background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;}",".column__text.rte,h2.column__heading.h5,h1.title--decorated.h3 {color: #e0f9f2;}"],"name":"Why Treeboard","settings":{"title":"Why Treeboard","sub-title":"","color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","align_text":"text-center","grid":3,"aspect_ratio":0.5,"width":"wrapper","padding_top":36,"padding_bottom":36}},"section_collection_PJypaQ":{"type":"section-collection","name":"Featured Products","settings":{"title":"Featured Products","description":"","collection":"featured-collection","grid":4,"limit":8,"enable_slider":true,"color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","show_view_all":false,"width":"wrapper","padding_top":36,"padding_bottom":36}},"section_columns_3HmPg4":{"type":"section-columns","blocks":{"text_block_HeYiLA":{"type":"text_block","settings":{"enable_image":true,"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/548c9d2eacefa9d1fe1b98ac9a556f157d24ded3.png","shape":"none","title":"Maple","text":"<p>The best maple cutting board starts with the tree itself. We source our hard maple from North American forests, choosing fallen trees and sustainably harvested wood.<br\/><\/p>","button_label":"Shop Maple","button_link":"shopify:\/\/collections\/cutting-boards-maple-cutting-boards","button_style":"btn","button_color":"btn--secondary"}},"text_block_fy9H8d":{"type":"text_block","settings":{"enable_image":true,"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/8e6004e5788f5bc796d7cf3f7310141d0713ae3d.png","shape":"none","title":"Cherry","text":"<p>Our cherry cutting boards are some of the most striking pieces we've ever made, and they just keep getting more beautiful over time.<\/p>","button_label":"Shop Cherry","button_link":"shopify:\/\/collections\/cutting-boards-cherry-cutting-boards","button_style":"btn","button_color":"btn--secondary"}},"text_block_DpTbwA":{"type":"text_block","settings":{"enable_image":true,"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/496f88260e4cd19d2b41bcf16097d4c3ed8026cb.png","shape":"none","title":"White Oak","text":"<p>Oak wood cutting boards offer a rare combination of hardness and character that few other woods can match.<\/p><p><\/p>","button_label":"Shop White Oak","button_link":"shopify:\/\/collections\/cutting-boards-oak-cutting-boards","button_style":"btn","button_color":"btn--secondary"}}},"block_order":["text_block_HeYiLA","text_block_fy9H8d","text_block_DpTbwA"],"custom_css":[".section-columns.palette--light.bg--neutral {background: #fef5e4;}"],"name":"Cutting Board By Woods","settings":{"title":"Cutting Boards by Wood","sub-title":"Each board is carved from a single piece — choose your favorite hardwood","color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","align_text":"text-center","grid":3,"aspect_ratio":1.1,"width":"wrapper","padding_top":36,"padding_bottom":36}},"16276923978337af16":{"type":"section-row","name":"Treeboard Founder","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/5dc327f6f682771c691e8fb462edabee439ade6b.png","shape":"none","aspect_ratio":0.7,"layout":"right","kicker":"<p>TREEBOARD'S FOUNDER<\/p>","heading":"<p>A Passion for Wood<\/p>","text_size":12,"sub-text":"<h3><strong>Will Mauldin<\/strong><\/h3>","text":"<p>Fell in love with trees and wooden objects in his early childhood. For years he worked as a journalist, mainly at The Wall Street Journal in Washington and Moscow. After a family tragedy struck in 2019, Will returned to his love of nature and began cutting up an already-fallen oak tree near his family's house in Maryland, launching a hobby and side job. He discovered that natural, solid slabs of hardwood can make beautiful cutting boards, bowls and other products, with only a limited role for humans or machinery.<\/p>","color_text_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","button_label":"Know More","button_link":"shopify:\/\/pages\/about","button_style":"btn--outline","button_color":"btn--neutral","color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","width":"wrapper","padding_top":56,"padding_bottom":56}},"tree_to_table_zmmBLc":{"type":"tree-to-table","blocks":{"feature_U3qDmp":{"type":"feature","settings":{"icon":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Group_657d5920-cd4d-43b4-8562-8f969ad6087b.png","label":"Glue Free"}},"feature_Mj4Hxt":{"type":"feature","settings":{"icon":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/fi_4352909_53c2420c-4734-459d-8a24-9e457cb1bcd6.png","label":"No fillers"}},"feature_bGEPrE":{"type":"feature","settings":{"icon":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/fi_9459151_1.png","label":"Just Solid Hardwood"}}},"block_order":["feature_U3qDmp","feature_Mj4Hxt","feature_bGEPrE"],"name":"Video with Text","settings":{"video_url":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=7G6NbemiAXQ","overlay_text":"","heading":"From Tree to Table","text":"<p>Handcrafted from solid, natural hardwood in our Maryland workshop, every Treeboard product is made to bring lasting beauty and everyday function to your kitchen. See what makes our boards different.<\/p>","button_label":"","button_link":"","bg_color":"#fef5e4","padding_top":40,"padding_bottom":40}},"1790597632be0b9d30":{"type":"apps","blocks":{"stamped_reviews_carousel_QwEdji":{"type":"shopify:\/\/apps\/stamped-reviews\/blocks\/carousel\/a103faaf-2125-4b0e-89fa-de5149736723","settings":{"title":"Real Reviews from Real Customers","auto_play":true,"take":30,"color_title":"","color_star":"","color_text":"","color_link":"","review_ids":"","product_ids":"","category":"","product_brand":"","tags":"","min_rating":"5","fill_empty":false,"random":false,"with_photos":false}}},"block_order":["stamped_reviews_carousel_QwEdji"],"settings":{"color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","width":"wrapper","padding_top":36,"padding_bottom":36}},"1646071720c6cd0da5":{"type":"section-blog","settings":{"title":"Recent Blogs","index_blog":"blog","limit":6,"grid":4,"aspect_ratio":1,"show_meta":true,"show_excerpt":true,"show_tags":false,"show_view_all":true,"color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","width":"wrapper","padding_top":36,"padding_bottom":36}},"164607169049e1a773":{"type":"section-accordion","blocks":{"164607169002ee0ce5-0":{"type":"text","settings":{"title":"Which is the better wood, hard maple or white oak?","content":"<p>It's largely a matter of personal preference, as these are the two most suitable North American hardwoods we've found for durable cutting boards. Maple is a lighter color and has finer pores. White oak (unlike red oak) has naturally sealed, rot-resistant grain that is coarser and of a darker hue, growing nearly as dark as walnut over time with linseed oil treatment. Oak is perhaps a bit more durable and less likely to show stains, although all treated boards resist stains, and stains can be removed.&nbsp;&nbsp;Read our&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/treeboard.com\/blogs\/blog\/which-wood-makes-the-best-cutting-boards-oak-or-maple\/\" title=\"https:\/\/treeboard.com\/blogs\/blog\/which-wood-makes-the-best-cutting-boards-oak-or-maple\/\">blog <\/a>for more on maple versus oak.<\/p>"}},"164607169002ee0ce5-1":{"type":"text","settings":{"title":"What about cherry?","content":"<p>Our cherry is stunningly beautiful, with classic grain that turns darker and redder over time with exposure to ambient light. Recent batches including either \"gum\" cherry that shows dark streaks of natural hardened resin or \"curly\" grain that shows a wavy pattern with chatoyance.<\/p><p>Cherry isn't as hard as white oak or hard maple, so it may show knife scratches more easily Overall cherry is better either for those with especially keen knife edges they're seeking to preserve on a softer cutting board, or for jobs where chopping isn't as important, such as serving appetizers or cheese.<\/p>"}},"164607169002ee0ce5-2":{"type":"text","settings":{"title":"Are your cutting boards one solid piece?","content":"<p>Yes. That's the whole point.<\/p>"}},"text_kFtJ6P":{"type":"text","settings":{"title":"Do they contain any glue, plastics or petrochemicals such as mineral oil?","content":"<p>No.<\/p>"}}},"block_order":["164607169002ee0ce5-0","164607169002ee0ce5-1","164607169002ee0ce5-2","text_kFtJ6P"],"name":"FAQ","settings":{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions","align_text":"text-center","text_size":2,"button_label":"View All FAQ","button_link":"shopify:\/\/pages\/faq","button_style":"btn","button_color":"btn--neutral","text_color":"text--neutral","bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","height":"use_screen_full","width":"wrapper","padding_top":36,"padding_bottom":64}},"1627692441e056071f":{"type":"section-newsletter","settings":{"enable_klaviyo":true,"title":"Newsletter","richtext":"<p>Get an extra $15 and be the first to know about our exclusive offers.<\/p>","success":"Success! Check your email for a confirmation.","text_color":"text--black","color_bg":"palette--light bg--neutral","button_color":"btn--neutral","button_style":"btn--soft","width":"wrapper","padding_top":0,"padding_bottom":0}}},"order":["section_slideshow_pJ6Yky","17893816474199607d","1627692309148c5268","section_hero_V6FGVm","blocks_FyPdq9","1627692301a4e021c0","section_columns_rwVxhW","section_collection_PJypaQ","section_columns_3HmPg4","16276923978337af16","tree_to_table_zmmBLc","1790597632be0b9d30","1646071720c6cd0da5","164607169049e1a773","1627692441e056071f"]}